ty is never set. But if the image has matte... wait, in the RGBAStrippedMethod, when does image->matte become true? Via extra samples. But the method RGBAStrippedMethod is selected only when QuantumTransferMode fails. And TIFFReadRGBAStrip always produces RGBA data regardless.\n\nHmm, so the bug: image->matte is true (extra samples declared), but the strip read doesn't set opacity? No, it does set opacity when matte.\n\nWait the MSan report says uninitialized value created by OpenCache allocation, used in VerticalFilter. VerticalFilter reads `p[j].opacity` when `source->matte` is true. So source (the read image) has matte true, but some pixels' opacity were never initialized. When would that happen? If image->matte true but the loop didn't set opacity for some pixels. In RGBAStrippedMethod, opacity is set for all pixels when matte. Hmm.\n\nUnless the image has matte but method isn't RGBAStrippedMethod for all... Actually the description says \"the opacity channel is not assured to be initialized in the RGBAStrippedMethod case\". Looking again:\n\n```c\nif (image->matte)\n  q->opacity=...;\n```\n\nIf image->matte is FALSE, opacity never initialized. But then VerticalFilter reads opacity only if source->matte. So how would source->matte be true at write time if read set it false? Because CloneImage... no.\n\nHmm, wait. Actually maybe the bug is the opposite: matte gets set true later (e.g., by SetImageAttribute alpha or by the writer), while the read pixels' opacity is uninitialized. Actually, TIFFGetR/G/B/A operate on strip_pixels from TIFFReadRGBAStrip. For a non-alpha image, TIFFReadRGBAStrip sets A=255. So opacity would be MaxRGB. But the code only assigns opacity when image->matte, leaving uninitialized for non-matte images.\n\nThen, the image is written as PTIF. WriteTIFFImage might set image->matte based on...? Hmm, actually in WritePTIFImage, CloneImage(image) copies matte flag. If matte false, ResizeImage's VerticalFilter uses the else branch and sets opacity